WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:05.640
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Doctor Who we got to see some serious medieval

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.380
robot shit go down.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.432
It was Mark Gatiss’ episode and I felt like
it was a marathon of references to classic

00:00:10.432 --> 00:00:11.970
who.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.110
Thank you to everyone who live tweeted the
episode with me, it’s always fun to do.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.779
I think we did an okay job of avoiding spoilers.

00:00:17.779 --> 00:00:20.380
If you’re just finding me for the first
time I do weekly Doctor Who videos.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.749
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:21.749 --> 00:00:25.230
I’m also doing a weekly giveaway I’ll
explain at the end of the video.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.411
So careful for spoilers from Robot of Sherwood
if you haven’t seen it yet, but here my

00:00:29.411 --> 00:00:32.079
top 5 moments…I’ll wait just a sec...okay.

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:33.440
Here we go

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.000
Number 5 - The Doctor’s Spoon

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.880
It had been a long time since i’d seen a
sword fighting episode of Doctor Who, I think

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.060
David Tennant did some sword fighting in Christmas
Invasion but since this was a Medieval episode

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.400
I got more of a King’s Demons, Time Warrior
vibe.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.000
I love how much he hates on Robin Hood from
the start.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.950
One of my favorite quotes from the episode
was the punch to the face line.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.310
I’m wondering if the series is building
to that.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.320
Eventually Capaldi just pops someone in the
face.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.590
That’s like the difference between Captain
Picard and Benjamin Sisko.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.670
Picard never punched Q in the face.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.750
I like thinking of Capaldi as the Benjamin
Sisko rough and tumble Doctor.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.200
Feels very much like the 9th Doctor.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:21.520
He always felt like he might jump out and
strangle villains to death.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.389
moving on to Number 4 - The Doctor Reacts
to Sherwood Forest

00:01:26.389 --> 00:01:29.621
Most of the first half of the episode was
him calling bullshit on everything and it

00:01:29.621 --> 00:01:30.810
was glorious.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:33.039
The archery contest was the icing on the cake.

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:35.189
If the whole tone of the robin hood scenes
felt weird.

00:01:35.189 --> 00:01:41.189
Like Tom Riley was “Over Performing”,
it was on purpose.

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:50.369
It was made to feel like Errol Flynn’s classic
Robin Hood because the robots created a real

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:56.140
life Robin Hood simulation to keep people
distracted.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:01.639
Like a giant holodeck Robin Hood episode.

00:02:01.639 --> 00:02:07.609
Oh wait, Next Gen totally did Robin Hood too.

00:02:07.609 --> 00:02:10.860
There are so many fandom streams being crossed
in my brain right now.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:16.970
I’ll talk a little more about the whole
vibe of the episode in my review, but Capaldi

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.510
just tromping across all the pomp and ceremony
was great.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:25.000
Like Clara was going squee all over her fantasy
and the doctor just wanted to stomp all over

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.000
it.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.850
I feel like you could take this as a meta
moment whenever some of the fandom hates an

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:30.850
episode or a character.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.250
They stomp all over it and call bullshit like
Capaldi did.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.440
Fun Fact: Steven Moffat claims he is THE Prototypical
Angry Doctor Who fan.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.050
Like in the years preceding the 2005 reboot
he was one of the biggest Angry Classic Who

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.930
fans complaining about the state of things.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.560
Which puts really puts this picture into context.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:51.960
But Number 3 - Everyone Just Shut It

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.950
Series 8 could be summed up in a series of
gifs of people telling each other to Shut

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:56.950
It.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.820
That should be capaldi’s catch phrase.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:02:59.820
“Shut It”.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:03.530
I love that Capaldi can set that kind of angry
tone in a scene and not make it feel off putting.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:07.140
Like it’s fun to watch everyone shushing
each other.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.070
Normally that’s something I’d get really
tired of fast.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:13.720
Part of me feels like the “Shut It’s”
are Moffat yelling back at the fandom.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:18.760
If anyone remembers, he used to be really
active on twitter around Series 6 but by the

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.560
time Series 7 started I think, he’d been
completely bullied off social media by crazy

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.190
people just shouting obscene things at him.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:29.390
I like the thought that he jumped at the chance
to cast a very scottish doctor who could speak

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:32.220
what Moffat wants to say to all his haters.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.970
Technically Mark Gatiss wrote the episode
but he and Moffat have been writing partners

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.360
for such a long time.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:40.220
You could also think of Capaldi as a very
angry version of Mycroft in the episode.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:45.240
Although in the Sherlock Holmes Canon, Mycroft
despises the idea of human contact so much,

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.160
he would never have left the TARDIS.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:55.910
I guess the TARDIS kind of is like a Time
Lord Diogenes Club

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:58.190
on to Number 2 - The Legend Of The Doctor

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:02.390
The metaphor for the Doctor as a Time Lord
Robin hood was a little on the nose, but I

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:03.750
still love the reference.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.530
He’s totally the Robin Hood of Gallifrey.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:08.660
I guess that makes Rassilon the Sheriff of
Nottingham?

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:12.160
Or maybe The Master?

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.840
I thought the real message was about the burden
of history.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:22.260
Like Tom Riley was telling the Doctor to not
be weighed down in the mire of his past mistakes.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.210
The darkness that he’s working through in
series 8.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:29.440
You could also see this as prophetic for the
Doctor’s own future.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.060
He’ll just turn into a legend.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.940
He kind of already is, being 2000 plus years
old and all.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.470
During the Matt Smith era the Legend was all
about him being a warrior, the most dangerous

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:41.780
man in the universe.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.901
I always wondered if that was because of the
historical things he’d already done, or

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:47.730
if the Silence knew he would eventually get
much more destructive.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:51.630
To be fair, he did blow up the universe in
order to save it.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:55.680
But the idea that Capaldi’s doctor could
be the fulfillment of the silence’s prophecy

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:56.680
is intriguing.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:00.130
The short explanation is that the prophecy
was just about Trenzalore and The Doctor helping

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.210
the Time Lords return.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:07.640
But let me know if you think Capaldi will
be the fullfilment of that, like Moffat will

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.650
carry the idea forward.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:13.700
He does that a lot.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:17.090
and my Number 1 moment - The Promised Land

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:20.780
There are a couple of things going on here
that made it hands down, the most fun part

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:21.830
of the episode for me.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:24.420
First, we see that The Promised land is in
fact a planet.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.000
Or what looks like a planet.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:33.419
It’s rendered in complete orange so we don’t
know more than that.

00:05:33.419 --> 00:05:37.110
When you consider this is the first episode
to not feature Missy, it makes me think that

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.650
the Promised Land is also the Nethersphere
is also Heaven.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.169
All three of those places are the same.

00:05:41.169 --> 00:05:45.700
Regardless of who or what Missy is, I think
we just got confirmation that Heaven is an

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.730
actual place, not just a mainframe.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:51.530
There was a big reference to Miss Evangelista
with the Ice Cream on the Spoon at the beginning

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:52.530
of the episode.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:57.490
So until I saw this picture I was still thinking
Heaven could be a digital place.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:01.140
Also, big Promised Land callback to the first
episode.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.490
The Robots in that story were also searching
for the Promised Land.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.520
It wasn’t clear if these robots were the
same type of robots in deep breath, the clockwork

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:08.520
droids.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.240
But part of me feels like they’re different.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:13.740
Which would mean that a lot of robots are
searching for the promised land.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:18.610
Missy is saving robots and people so it’s
still a little confusing as to who is ‘allowed’

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.060
into the promised land.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.750
So far it seems like missy is only saving
people that sacrifice themselves in the name

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:24.860
of the doctor.

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:27.960
But she doesn’t seem like she’s saving
them out of spite to the doctor.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.020
The other big moment was when the Second Doctor
flashed on the screen.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:36.230
In real life in 1953, he became the first
actor to portray Robin Hood on TV.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:37.770
That was before he became the doctor.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.310
So this picture was taken when he was much
younger.

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:43.730
But let me know what your favorite moment
was and let me know what your favorite promised

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:44.730
land theory is!

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:51.310
Here’s a couple of the bigger references
I spotted in the episode.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.950
Feel free to add any if there’s something
you think I missed.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:54.992
I’m just going to list the biggest ones:

00:06:54.992 --> 00:06:56.430
There’s the Spoon and the ice cream.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.979
Spoons were a big thing for the seventh doctor
when he first started his run.

00:06:59.979 --> 00:07:04.060
Ice Cream was a recurring subject during the
Matt Smith years and during Silence in the

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.060
Library.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:08.699
Evangelista whispered Ice Cream before she
faded away.

00:07:08.699 --> 00:07:13.010
The Medieval Robots theme of the episode was
a huge callback to Time Warrior from the Third

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:14.010
Doctor’s Run.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:17.850
That was Sarah Jane’s first big episode
as a companion and the story was somewhat

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:18.850
similar.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:22.760
In that episode, a Sontaran gives a local
robber baron a robot knight while he tries

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.820
to repair his spaceship.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:28.510
The fifth doctor also went back to medieval
times in King’s Demons.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:33.540
It featured the master and introduced Kamelion
who went on to become a robot companion.

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:37.050
Lots of Medieval Robots in Doctor Who history.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:41.110
Visually it felt like the arrow shots in bullet
time were a reference to the Kevin Costner

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:47.680
Robin Hood movie.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.080
If you ever watched the Mel Brooks parody,
Men in Tights, they did a version of this

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:56.610
where the arrow just goes around doing ridiculous
random things before finding it’s target.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:58.979
The voices of the Robots sounded very Borg
like.

00:07:58.979 --> 00:08:01.330
Maybe there’s a star trek fan on the crew?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:08.610
There were a lot of later references to similar
things in the third and fifth doctor episodes,

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.860
like the sword fighting, arrow shooting and
alien spaceship.

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:14.130
I’m sure there were a lot more I missed.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:18.449
But feel free to add any big classic who references
I didn’t mention.

00:08:18.449 --> 00:08:22.860
There were lot of minor Matt Smith references,
like Clara trying to explain when she started

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:23.860
believing in heroes.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:26.759
Right after that the doctor flipped the 11th
doctor’s sonic in the air.

00:08:26.759 --> 00:08:36.169
Overall I gave the episode a B, I loved that
the story turned into the simulation trying

00:08:36.169 --> 00:08:39.640
to get Capaldi to reaffirm his own sense of
self.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:43.830
I think part of those chalkboard equations
are Capaldi trying to figure out his own self

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.700
in addition to finding Gallifrey.

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:51.450
In practice a lot of the Doctor Robin Hood
banter drug the the pace down.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:55.790
I don’t expect every episode to be as quick
as Into the Dalek or Deep Breath but Robot

00:08:55.790 --> 00:09:01.800
of Sherwood felt a little out of place.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.600
We were already told that series 8 would feature
more stand-alone episodes.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.570
And this was very much a stand alone.

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:10.830
I feel like they weren’t sure where to air
this episode so rather than have it slow the

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:13.601
pace of the Missy story down later on, they
wanted to get it out of the way early.

00:09:13.601 --> 00:09:15.390
I think once we get to the halfway mark in
terms of episodes, the Missy Nethersphere

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:16.430
plot will start to dominate more and more.

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:18.520
And putting robin hood in the middle of that
would just be weird.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:23.321
Tom Riley and Ben Miller were great as an
Errol Flynn version of Robin Hood and the

00:09:23.321 --> 00:09:24.570
sheriff of nottigham.

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:28.790
I was bummed that they didn’t definitively
answer the Robin Hood robot question.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:33.100
It seemed like Capaldi was saying he was manufactured
as part of the narrative disguise the robots

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.100
were using.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.990
But he seemed like he was flesh and blood.

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:39.350
And at the end of the episode, he was still
walking around believing he was the real life

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:40.350
Robin Hood.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.350
Very confusing.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:46.630
There was a real life robin hood in history,
but the real story is very different.

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:51.510
King Richard the Lionheart almost bankrupt
england with the crusades, and his brother

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:54.279
the prince actually tried to save the kingdom.

00:09:54.279 --> 00:09:58.730
So in real life Prince John wasn’t evil.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.920
The ending with Maid Marion was also unnecessary.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:10.080
Here’s what I think happened, the Doctor
time traveled picked her up and dropped her

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.500
off before leaving again.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:14.000
And she just seemed to appear because we were
seeing things from the perspective of Tom

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.000
Riley.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.970
The other explanation is that Robin Hood really
is a construct and the Doctor, as thanks,

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.490
made a marion construct to give Robin Hood
closure.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:28.060
You can let me know where you fall on the
Robin Hood as real person or robot but I still

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.400
enjoyed the episode a lot despite a few pacing
and logic issues.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:34.560
Usually when stories don’t make sense like
this, it’s because scenes explaining things

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.510
get cut out at the last minute.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:41.320
My next bonus video will be my favorite fictional
and historical doctor who characters, like

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:46.860
when the doctor talks about famous people
real or not real he’s been with.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:47.970
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:50.930
That will post next, tomorrow I’ll post
my Q&amp;A, so you should have plenty of time

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.680
to re-watch the episodes and ask questions.

00:10:52.680 --> 00:11:00.700
I’ll also announce the giveaway winner for
this week in that video.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.950
Right now click here for the bonus video I’ll
add the annotation in a couple hours when

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:04.950
I post it.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.100
And click here for the Q&amp;A.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.750
I’ll update that tomorrow to with the right
link.

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:11.910
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:14.640
High Fives!

